5151311378f4670c7cf7274ce2e1c017ca9b7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131397" :question/id #uuid "449f656d-2e72-51b8-aaf5-0f5765ff88e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131397" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z\\ge 0.17).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5199\\,$ | $\\,0.5239\\,$ | $\\,0.5279\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5596\\,$ | $\\,0.5636\\,$ | $\\,0.5675\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ | $\\,0.6026\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z\\ge 0.17).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/759e123d5c61321e78b085260a14d5ae98a54b724b82b06cdecc46ff28072b8b.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge 0.17) & =1-P(Z<0.17) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.17)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/83ab5f91c5ee81eeb4c31b42558af5c46cb59d74603b30913ab80dadeafc3317.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(0.17)=0.5675.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge 0.17) & =1-Φ(0.17) \\\\  & =1-0.5675 \\\\  & =0.4325.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131397/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e376bffa-02ae-5575-af2c-4ad5e703f9fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131397"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131399/selection/f5ab26c24f63242e0