131399" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z\\ge -2.15).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.0162\\,$ | $\\,0.0158\\,$ | $\\,0.0154\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0207\\,$ | $\\,0.0202\\,$ | $\\,0.0197\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.0262\\,$ | $\\,0.0256\\,$ | $\\,0.0250\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z\\ge -2.15).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/f814b532742940206d119c1aa30746b128ab6ede249128e55fc949a1051220c9.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -2.15) & =1-P(Z<-2.15) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-2.15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/9e2cf363bd0732c4669c4653d83f505826af605f2bc719a4f39135d233456b57.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-2.15)=0.0158.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -2.15) & =1-Φ(-2.15) \\\\  & =1-0.0158 \\\\  & =0.9842.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131399/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e376bffa-02ae-5575-af2c-4ad5e703f9fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131399"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94151/selection/ba3bb3796bfe1caef2fbbe45e77afd8c6c2af2f16a9b8a58497adce24d8ea81d" :answer/id #uuid "bb0addc0-4619-5414-bd6a-e420ef8fab7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3856" :db/ensure 