to compute $P(Z\\ge -1.32).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/d89bd5f38fdf4c952146dde8cd01207167c92cab07290742d229ceb0f4cf5712.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.32) & =1-P(Z<-1.32) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.32)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/0959a3c48bf70d10f24d85cd98bcd0703db4765ba5349d02896e18104c3f98a7.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.32)=0.0934.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.32) & =1-Φ(-1.32) \\\\  & =1-0.0934 \\\\  & =0.9066.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131400/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e376bffa-02ae-5575-af2c-4ad5e703f9fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131400"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131518/selection/bdb968ce8332b1ce1df13003c5d5a7ae690bebe7d49e427e22e8928452413339" :answer/id #uuid "ad8588bb-3d4b-58e6-927b-b75ae0ba4685" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3690" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131518/selection/249096166a7f94981946c113f1d01cd0e33fbda6b95699aa704ccb6ea3c4c4c5" :answer/id #uuid "ba796ee2-cab1-544e-b94d-8278e26e5944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4154" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131518/selection/81ea87904f1069475ab03c84343971e017b9d1c7215988940f1828e08bd63e4e" :answer/id #uuid "f247de43-2d95-5fbf-98f6-be4fca3b812c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3934" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131518/selection/6821da27d4dee8059355b30b771ee8b7bcb21da787bc242b6d