,0.9452\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5000\\,$ | $\\,0.5040\\,$ | $\\,0.5080\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5398\\,$ | $\\,0.5438\\,$ | $\\,0.5478\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.5832\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9192\\,$ | $\\,0.9207\\,$ | $\\,0.9222\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9332\\,$ | $\\,0.9345\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9452\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(0.1<Z<1.5).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/806631e940119accaf9fa2dd9e52e59f4ae16480f237c2bb67ddc7796e4967c0.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.1<Z<1.5) & =P(Z<1.5)-P(Z\\le 0.1) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.5)-P(Z\\le 0.1) \\\\  & =Φ(1.5)-Φ(0.1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.1) & =0.5398 \\\\ Φ(1.5) & =0.9332\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.1<Z<1.5) & =Φ(1.5)-Φ(0.1) \\\\  & =0.9332-0.5398 \\\\  & =0.3934.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131518/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "607e0800-870c-5271-9220-0489d9c5b891"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131518"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131521/selection/6a6d872d4a6f7a0af88d6612ba5d7e77d9af77d71c92917e3a3b02a50835a7a3" :answer/id #uuid "4f5ea166-7526-56b8-af2d-57be2077b34d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1378" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]