ute $P(-1.99<Z<-0.99).$\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0192\\,$ | $\\,0.0188\\,$ | $\\,0.0183\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.0244\\,$ | $\\,0.0239\\,$ | $\\,0.0233\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0307\\,$ | $\\,0.0301\\,$ | $\\,0.0294\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1423\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.1379\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1660\\,$ | $\\,0.1635\\,$ | $\\,0.1611\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.1922\\,$ | $\\,0.1894\\,$ | $\\,0.1867\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0192\\,$ | $\\,0.0188\\,$ | $\\,0.0183\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.0244\\,$ | $\\,0.0239\\,$ | $\\,0.0233\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0307\\,$ | $\\,0.0301\\,$ | $\\,0.0294\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1423\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.1379\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1660\\,$ | $\\,0.1635\\,$ | $\\,0.1611\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.1922\\,$ | $\\,0.1894\\,$ | $\\,0.1867\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-1.99<Z<-0.99).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/8dc66c8ceed4366688dc040104eaece3d251ecb9f72d9aae0827ead3fe933570.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.99<Z<-0.99) & =P(Z<-0.99)-P(Z\\le -1.99) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.99)-P(Z\\le -1.99) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.99)-Φ(-1.99).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.99) & =0.0233 \\\\ Φ(-0.99) & =0.1611\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.99<Z<-0.99) & =Φ(-0.99)-Φ(-1.99) \\\\  & =0.1611-0.0233 \\\\  & =0.1378.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131521/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "607e0800-870c-5271-9220-0489d9c5b891"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131521"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334484/field-1/3da5c1d039b57c5016b97a7d9935cdb3927a811891ea75b3ec333f3ad7339a73" :answer/id #uuid "9f20f107-94a7-5753-b465-69e642e03804" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2498" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334484/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "386b646a-bd53-5754-809b-5f9a38e47d29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-334484/field-1/3da5c1d039b57c5016b97a7d9935cdb3927a811891ea75b3ec333f3ad7339a73" :answer-field/choices ["q-334484/field-1/3da5c1d039b57c5016b97a7d9935cdb3927a811891ea75b3ec333f3ad7339a73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334484" :question/id #uuid "11265fa8-1f94-59fd-bbab-fa021bc7680e" :question/math-academy-id "q-334484" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.92<Z<-0.18).$ Use the tables below and do not round your answer.\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1841\\,$ | $\\,0.1814\\,$ | $\\,0.1788\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2119\\,$ | $\\,0.2090\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ | $\\,0.3859\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | $\\,0.4247\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.4721\\,$ | $\\,0.4681\\,$ | $\\,0.4641\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1841\\,$ | $\\,0.1814\\,$ | $\\,0.1788\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2119\\,$ | $\\,0.2090\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ | $\\,0.3859\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | $\\,0.4247\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.4721\\,$ | $\\,0.4681\\,$ | $\\,0.4641\\,$ |\n\n$P(-0.92<Z<-0.18)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.92<Z<-0.18).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/34132169270b3259fb1be909f7aea2474e4dff1375603e9b9a75e013900f6340.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.92<Z<-0.18) & =P(Z<-0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.92) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.92) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.18)-Φ(-0.92).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.92) & =0.1788 \\\\ Φ(-0.18) & =0.4286\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.92<Z<-0.18) & =Φ(-0.18)-Φ(-0.92) \\\\  & =0.4286-0.1788 \\\\  & =0.2498.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334484/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "607e0800-870c-5271-9220-0489d9c5b891"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334484"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94194/selection/ba5f4d4006d2e27625a48b6fae7583ca2d44d0e660d6e2d5dbb3165a29503013" :answer/id #uuid "8feb120d-d218-5fbc-88c7-feaa019fc31d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2632" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-941