 $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1151\\,$ | $\\,0.1131\\,$ | $\\,0.1112\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1357\\,$ | $\\,0.1335\\,$ | $\\,0.1314\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.3085\\,$ | $\\,0.3050\\,$ | $\\,0.3015\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.3409\\,$ | $\\,0.3372\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3821\\,$ | $\\,0.3783\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1151\\,$ | $\\,0.1131\\,$ | $\\,0.1112\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1357\\,$ | $\\,0.1335\\,$ | $\\,0.1314\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.3085\\,$ | $\\,0.3050\\,$ | $\\,0.3015\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.3409\\,$ | $\\,0.3372\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3821\\,$ | $\\,0.3783\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-1.2<Z<-0.31).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/46b71217fcee1d130b3778ce2cd101aac9814870b71683656987d476e71412c1.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.2<Z<-0.31) & =P(Z<-0.31)-P(Z\\le -1.2) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.31)-P(Z\\le -1.2) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.31)-Φ(-1.2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.2) & =0.1151 \\\\ Φ(-0.31) & =0.3783\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.2<Z<-0.31) & =Φ(-0.31)-Φ(-1.2) \\\\  & =0.3783-0.1151 \\\\  & =0.2632.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94194/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "607e0800-870c-5271-9220-0489d9c5b891"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94194"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94195"] :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(0.70<Z<0.92).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(0.70<Z<0.92).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/3eb46852c53e4fa13aaa29c31623153bfef604d138f15c6da67732d5730b785f.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.70<Z<0.92) & =P(Z<0.92)-P(Z\\le 0.70) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.92)-P(Z\\le 0.70) \\\\  & =Φ(0.92)-Φ(0.70)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.70) & =0.7580 \\\\ Φ(0.92) & =0.8212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.7<Z<0.92) & =Φ(0.92)-Φ(0.70) \\\\  & =0.8212-0.7580 \\\\  & =0.0632.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13266"] :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z < -1.54).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.03 \\,$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -1.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.063 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0618 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0606 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0764 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0749 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0735 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0918 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0901 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0885 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "If $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ then by the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq z) = \\Phi(z).\n$$\n\nAlso, since $Z$ is continuous, \n\n$$\nP(Z <             -1.54) = P(Z \\leq -1.54) = \\Phi(-1.54).\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/32adba8c3a4324eccce9b4ccbdb32ab2c2c3c76c3ad8216568b58f8bec0c8c46.png)\n\nNow, we determine the value of $\\Phi(-1.54)$ from the table:\n\n- We first select the row that corresponds to $-1.5$ and the column that corresponds to $0.04.$\n\n- Then, we take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.03 \\,$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -1.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.063 \\,$ | $\\color{blue}\\, 0.0618 \\,$ | $\\,0.0606\\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0764 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0749 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0735 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0918 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0901 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0885 \\,$ |\n\nTherefore, according to the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq  -1.54) = \\Phi(-1.54) = 0.0618\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13267"] :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z \\geq -1.16).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -1.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0901 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0885 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0869 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1075 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1056 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1038 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.1 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1271 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1251 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1230 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z \\geq -1.16).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/cac32ab36217820b63574e011488721bf57652fa63b4cbb7e5029fb54ce26243.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq z) = \\Phi(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $\\Phi(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.16) & =1-P(Z<-1.16) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/48adcb6bd3b0d12b9bc935b2414d615e0014d905b89a9f7d632306cd30f08580.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\\Phi(-1.16) =  0.1230.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.16) & =1-Φ(-1.16) \\\\  & =1-0.1230 \\\\  & =0.8770.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13268"] :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.48 <              Z <              1.18).$\n\n| | $z$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2843 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2810 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2776 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3192 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3156 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3121 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3557 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3520 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3483 \\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8577 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8599 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8621 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.1 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8790 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8810 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8830 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8980 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8997 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9015 \\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2843 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2810 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2776 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3192 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3156 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3121 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3557 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3520 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3483 \\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8577 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8599 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8621 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.1 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8790 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8810 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8830 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8980 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8997 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9015 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.48 <     Z <   1.18).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/f9011a3355b8261e153842a43be45e9bb07240d88421e37f7297a7d0f807e101.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq z) = \\Phi(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\\Phi(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.48<Z<1.18) & =P(Z<1.18)-P(Z\\le -0.48) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.18)-P(Z\\le -0.48) \\\\  & =Φ(1.18)-Φ(-0.48)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.48) & =0.3156 \\\\ Φ(1.18) & =0.8810\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.48<Z<1.18) & =Φ(1.18)-Φ(-0.48) \\\\  & =0.8810-0.3156 \\\\  & =0.5654.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
